# Neon PostgreSQL connection string
# Create a project at https://neon.tech, copy the connection string from the Neon Console,
# and paste it below. Keep this file out of version control — copy to .env instead.
#
# Neon example (use the exact string from your Neon Dashboard):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://refdesk_owner:password@ep-cool-shadow-a1b2c3d4-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require"
#
# Notes:
# - Use the pooler connection string for serverless / Prisma (Neon Dashboard → Connection Details)
# - Always include sslmode=require
# - Never hard-code credentials in source code
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"
